      "spec": "{API_000003 supplies nationality, name, passport_number, passport_expiration_date, date_of_birth, gender, username, password, confirm_password, email and agreed_to_terms for an unauthenticated visitor; the API has already received them from the registration form} pass all eleven supplied values unchanged to ValidateRegistration and inspect its result. {when ValidateRegistration returns valid=false, return username=null, session_id=null and error equal to ValidateRegistration.output.error, and create no account and no session} {when ValidateRegistration returns valid=true, locally compute a password hash from input.password using the application password-hashing routine, locally generate a new account identifier and a new session identifier, persist one new user_account row holding the generated account identifier, input.nationality, input.name, input.passport_number, input.passport_expiration_date, input.date_of_birth, input.gender, input.username, input.email and the computed password hash in place of the plain password, and persist one new session row with the generated session identifier associated with that new account so the session resolves to the account as required by ResolveActiveSession; perform both inserts in one transaction; return username=input.username, session_id=the generated session identifier and error=null so API_000003 can set the session cookie and respond with the saved username} {if persisting either row fails, roll back both inserts, return error=null username and null session_id with an error description, and leave no account and no session} {frame: on failure no user_account row and no session row are created; on success exactly one user_account row and one session row are created; rows of other accounts and sessions are left unchanged; agreed_to_terms itself is not persisted; no clear-text password is stored or returned} {callees: none besides validation for storage; the account and session inserts are executed directly against user_account and session data} {downstream data requirements for the storage pass: insert a user_account with all validated profile fields and a hashed password returning its generated identifier, and insert a session linked to that account returning its generated identifier, both participating in one transaction}. ",
