      "spec": "{the visitor has entered the registration fields and clicks the \"Next step\" button while no submission is in flight} clears any previous error (registration_error_message = null), sets registration_submitting = true, and calls POST /api/register with the body built from the current form state: nationality, name, passport_number, passport_expiration_date, date_of_birth, gender, username, password, confirm_password, email and agreed_to_terms (true only when the consent checkbox is checked). All requirement validations (required fields, 2-100 non-whitespace characters for name, 6-30 ASCII letters/digits/hyphens for passport_number, date_of_birth earlier than today, passport_expiration_date later than today, 3-32 ASCII letters/digits/hyphens/underscores for username, valid email of at most 254 characters, 12-128 character password containing uppercase, lowercase, digit and special character, identical confirm_password, unique username and case-insensitively unique email) are enforced by the RegisterAccount API, so the handler does not bypass them. {on a response carrying an error} sets registration_submitting = false and sets registration_error_message to the returned error text, keeping the visitor on /register with the entered values and creating no account or session. {on a response carrying username} the API has already persisted the account and session and set the session cookie, so sets registration_submitting = false and navigates the visitor to / where the header load resolves the session and displays the saved username as text with the \"Sign out\" link} {a successful submission leaves registration_error_message null; a failed submission leaves the form data, account and session state otherwise unchanged}",
